Last night I reached my goal of ascending every possible Wizard
combination (elf, gnome, orc, human neu&cha) with a chaotic human on
NAO. The game was ridiculously easy because I found a wand of wishing
on level 2. I got the requisite charging scrolls and SDSM. Found
randomly generated speed boots and bag of holding (pre-Sokoban!), so
used the rest of the charges on magic markers and gauntlets (power at
first, later dexterity). Meanwhile I found *another* wand of wishing
in a chest: 0:3. That and the Castle wand (also 0:3!) never got
zapped. Before ascending, I got two more wishes from thrones, found a
magic lamp, and by the way smoky potions were extra healing so I
probably could have gotten even more.

I pondered what else to do with all of my spare wishes, but I really
couldn't think of anything else I needed to ascend, and I didn't want
to suffer YASD while goofing around. I'm not the type that wishes for
artifacts (never for quest artifacts, and very rarely for weapons),
but I suppose I could have tried for some, though a number were
randomly generated or otherwise created in this game; Excalibur in a
bones pile, Vorpal Blade in Vlad's in place of the usual long sword
(good; I wouldn't face a player monster with it on Astral at least),
Ogresmasher as a death drop (?!?), an Aleax with Demonbane, and I
think at least one other randomly lying around. I never did get
Stormbringer, but didn't care; Magicbane and magic missile/finger of
death were more than sufficient.

So after my usual sac-and-poly fest (there were also several altars,
including one on the same level as Ludios, very handy for branch-
porting) I got bored and finished the game, with two 0:3 wands of
wishing and a magic lamp still in my inventory. The end was very
anticlimactic; dropping enough to be unburdened made for the fastest
Planes run in recent memory, and the first altar was the right one (I
checked twice because I couldn't believe my luck).

So if you'd been in this situation, what would you have wished for?


